@startuml

title Marketing Site — Delivery Pipeline (Threat Model View)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam wrapWidth 240
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #666666
skinparam noteBorderColor #CC6600
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF3E0
skinparam sequenceDividerBorderColor #333333
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #E8E8E8

actor "Marketing\nTeam" as Marketing
actor "Security\nTeam" as SecTeam
actor "Production\nReviewer" as Reviewer

box "External (out of scope)" #F5F5F5
  participant "Webflow\n(Platform)" as Webflow #LightGray
  participant "SharePoint\n(Storage)" as SharePoint #LightGray
end box

box "GitHub: CordaXYZ-Marketing-Site" #EAF4EA
  participant "main\nbranch" as Main
  participant "GitHub\nActions" as GHActions #LightYellow
  participant "staging\nbranch" as Staging
  participant "production\nbranch" as Prod
end box

box "Cloudflare Pages (out of scope)" #F5F5F5
  participant "Staging\nSite" as CFStaging #LightGray
  participant "Production\nSite" as CFProd #LightGray
end box

== CONTENT CREATION & SHAREPOINT HANDOFF ==

Marketing -> Webflow : Design and publish site
activate Webflow
Webflow --> Marketing : Export static site as ZIP
deactivate Webflow

note over Marketing, SharePoint #FFCCCC
  **MALICIOUS_CONTENT_INJECTION**
  No hash/signature binds Webflow export to SharePoint ZIP.
  Compromised insider can substitute arbitrary content.
end note

Marketing -> SharePoint : Upload ZIP\n+ notify Security Team

== REPOSITORY INGESTION ==

SecTeam -> SharePoint : Download ZIP\n(manual review)
SharePoint --> SecTeam : webflow-export.zip

note over SecTeam, Main #FFCCCC
  **WORKFLOW_FILE_TAMPERING**
  GH action workflows lives on main without signed-commit
  protection. A compromised dev can disable security gates
  or add secret-exfiltration steps.
end note

SecTeam -> Main : git commit webflow-exports/<export>.zip\n(triggers webflow-import.yml)

Main -> GHActions : webflow-import.yml triggered\n(push to webflow-exports/**)
activate GHActions

note over GHActions #FFCCCC
  **ZIP_PATH_TRAVERSAL**
  A crafted ZIP can write files outside the
  expected directory, overwriting security
  gate scripts mid-run.
end note

GHActions -> GHActions : Extract ZIP → dist/\nValidate dist/index.html present

note over GHActions #FFCCCC
  **THIRD_PARTY_ACTION_SUPPLY_CHAIN**
  External pipeline tools are referenced by
  mutable version tags. A compromised publisher
  gains full access to repository secrets.
end note

GHActions -> Staging : git push --force origin staging\n(dist/ content)
GHActions -> SecTeam : Slack: webflow import succeeded
deactivate GHActions

== STAGING CI ==

Staging -> GHActions : ci-staging.yml triggered\n(dispatch from webflow-import)
activate GHActions

GHActions -> GHActions : 1 — domain-scan\n(scripts/check-domains.py)

note over GHActions #E8FFE8
  **DOMAIN_SCAN_CONTROL (in place)**
  Blocks pipeline if dist/ references any domain
  absent from the CSP allowlist.
end note

note over GHActions #FFCCCC
  **DOMAIN_SCAN_EVASION**
  Static scan misses inline JS fetch calls,
  CSS exfiltration, and obfuscated Base64 URLs.
  Malicious content can pass this gate.
end note

GHActions -> CFStaging : Await Cloudflare staging deploy\n(poll STAGING_URL until HTTP 2xx)
CFStaging --> GHActions : HTTP 200 — staging live

GHActions -> CFStaging : 2 — link-check (lychee)\n3 — DAST (ZAP baseline passive scan)
CFStaging --> GHActions : HTTP responses

note over GHActions #E8FFE8
  **DAST_STAGING_GATE (in place)**
  ZAP passive scan detects XSS, insecure forms,
  and CSP violations on the live staging site.
end note

GHActions -> SecTeam : Slack: staging CI result\n(pass = ready to promote | fail = blocked)
deactivate GHActions

== PRODUCTION PROMOTION ==

note over SecTeam, GHActions #FFCCCC
  **SCHEDULED_PROMOTION_ABUSE**
  A promotion can be triggered automatically
  without Security Team action, enabling
  deployments outside monitored hours.
end note

SecTeam -> GHActions : Dispatch promote.yml\n(or scheduled-promote.yml fires)
activate GHActions

GHActions -> GHActions : verify-staging\n(latest ci-staging must be conclusion: success)

note over GHActions, Reviewer #E8FFE8
  **PRODUCTION_GATE_APPROVAL (in place)**
  One reviewer other than the initiator must approve
  on production-gate before every merge.
end note

GHActions -> Reviewer : GitHub UI: request production-gate approval
Reviewer --> GHActions : Approve

GHActions -> Prod : Merge staging → production\n(fast-forward or merge commit)

note over Prod #E8FFE8
  **BRANCH_PROTECTION_PRODUCTION (in place)**
  Production write-restricted to github-actions.
  No human can push directly.
end note

GHActions -> SecTeam : Slack: promotion initiated

== PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT & VALIDATION ==

Prod -> CFProd : Cloudflare auto-deploys\nproduction branch on push
CFProd --> GHActions : HTTP 200 (production live)

GHActions -> CFProd : smoke-test (lychee)\n+ DAST (ZAP baseline passive scan)
CFProd --> GHActions : HTTP responses

note over GHActions, SecTeam #FFCCCC
  **GH_ACTIONS_SECRET_EXFILTRATION**
  Pipeline credentials are available to all jobs.
  A leaked webhook enables fake Slack notifications
  to manipulate gate decisions.
end note

GHActions -> SecTeam : Slack: PRODUCTION live\n(commit SHA, approvers, link-check, DAST)
deactivate GHActions

@enduml
